A||||2||mshill||Gas gauge, gas tank woes...||||13||
Z||000000||mshill||08-18-2000||11:56 AM||||I was driving my 86SE yesterday with the gas gauge showing about two lines above empty when I feel it miss.  I quickly got off the freeway and sure enough it starts missing again.  I knew the gauge was off a little but not this much.  Anyway, I cruise into an Exxon station just before I run out completely.<P>So, I count my blessings and fill it up, but it only takes 8.9 gallons total even after topping it off.  I thought that these tanks were 10+ gallons?  It really sucks to only get 190 miles out of a tank.  Yes, I only get 21 MPG out of my V6 cause I have a +1 cam in it.||||reg||13
Z||000001||Rodrv6||08-18-2000||04:25 PM||||The tank is 10.6 gallon capacity,(1984-86) BUT if your's is like mine the pump will shut off with 2 or 3 gallons of room left.  The only way to really fill it is to dribble the last couple of gallons in very slowly.  I asked about this a couple of months ago on this forum, and it seems to be a common problem.  It is frustrating not to be able to easily use all the space available!<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE<p>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 08-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierodave||08-18-2000||10:32 PM||||You guys ever look into one of the tanks?  geeez  there is about 20 different baffels in it  i took a tank out of that Cal GT I parted and couldn't even pour the last quart or so out, even with the sending unit out!  upside down and it still had gas in it!  I guess thats why we don't hear the gas slosh around between the seats!.  It looks like some type of fuel cell!  it also lools like the sending unit/pick up could be adjusted to sit lower in the tank, I used a ruler and I bet 1 more inch lower it could go into the tank,  and you still could never hit the actual bottom I think because of the plastic looking stuff in there!<BR>FD ||||reg||1
